WEBVTT

00:01.720 --> 00:05.430
That's Jonas's signal. 
But he rang it last night, too.

00:05.810 --> 00:07.750
Is he having the duke 
look at something again?

00:10.040 --> 00:11.080
Right then!

00:13.700 --> 00:16.010
As I am so amazing, I'll go scout things out!

00:18.020 --> 00:20.290
I added more folds to the drapery of her dress.

00:20.960 --> 00:23.320
And I've added openwork designs to the hems.

00:24.010 --> 00:25.990
That should make it 
more accurate than before.

00:27.350 --> 00:28.400
Mithril?

00:28.400 --> 00:29.610
How did things look?

00:33.330 --> 00:35.050
What's this? Challe?

00:35.050 --> 00:38.060
He was trying to enter Jonas's room,

00:38.060 --> 00:40.170
so I caught him before 
he could do anything dubious.

00:41.510 --> 00:44.060
Bah. I wasn't trying to do 
anything suspicious.

00:44.060 --> 00:46.400
I was thinking of playing 
a little trick on him, that's all!

00:46.760 --> 00:47.860
A trick?

00:47.860 --> 00:50.820
He looked incredibly depressed, 
which made me really happy!

00:50.820 --> 00:53.260
What? He was depressed?

00:54.490 --> 01:02.510
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but…</i>

01:09.210 --> 01:11.930
<i>It's all right</i>

01:11.930 --> 01:15.770
<i>Even alone, I'll be fine, but…</i>

01:15.770 --> 01:22.270
<i>You know, the truth is
 that no one is alone</i>

01:22.270 --> 01:28.850
<i>Things like happiness, 
loneliness, and even anxiety…</i>

01:28.850 --> 01:38.170
<i>We are born to savor all those things</i>

01:38.610 --> 01:41.830
<i>A single spoonful of sparkles</i>

01:41.830 --> 01:44.950
<i>Transforms everything into smiles</i>

01:45.230 --> 01:52.060
<i>That could be what I secretly wished for…</i>

01:52.060 --> 01:54.760
<i>That miracle</i>

01:55.010 --> 02:01.720
<i>We're each searching for
 our most precious treasures</i>

02:01.720 --> 02:08.020
<i>That's what our journey is for</i>

02:08.020 --> 02:15.140
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but...</i>

02:15.140 --> 02:23.370
<i>Each moment that passes before me
 shall be spun from hope</i>

02:24.840 --> 02:25.960
Is it finished?

02:25.960 --> 02:27.980
Yes. I think it's done now.

02:27.980 --> 02:29.460
Then we should signal, too, Anne.

02:30.270 --> 02:31.920
Yes. Would you?

02:35.960 --> 02:39.240
It hasn't changed. 
It's the same as yesterday.

02:39.240 --> 02:40.130
What?

02:41.780 --> 02:42.870
You...

02:43.900 --> 02:45.690
and that artisan below us...

02:46.250 --> 02:48.600
neither of you understand a thing.

02:49.260 --> 02:50.570
Give it form!

02:53.940 --> 02:55.560
What does he mean?

02:58.460 --> 03:01.720
What about it didn't work?

03:01.720 --> 03:03.660
He even said that it hadn't changed.

03:04.030 --> 03:09.360
Perhaps the Duke of Philax isn't simply 
looking for a splendid sugar confection.

03:09.360 --> 03:10.200
What?

03:10.650 --> 03:12.370
If it were only a splendid sugar confection,

03:12.880 --> 03:15.920
then yours should serve 
more than well enough.

03:15.920 --> 03:17.340
Hmm...

03:22.410 --> 03:26.060
Next, let's try making something 
from a different direction...

03:26.750 --> 03:28.580
something more realistic.

03:39.750 --> 03:42.060
That's really different from the last one.

03:44.280 --> 03:45.690
Is it finished now?

03:45.690 --> 03:46.570
Yes...

03:47.420 --> 03:50.460
but I'm going to go look 
at the painting one last time.

03:57.540 --> 03:59.520
Where are you going, Anne?

03:59.520 --> 04:02.470
Where? To go see the paintings, that's all.

04:03.890 --> 04:05.760
You're still working on something?

04:05.760 --> 04:07.060
So are you, aren't you?

04:07.390 --> 04:09.540
I can't make anything.

04:10.060 --> 04:13.880
I have <i>no</i> idea what he means by what he says!

04:14.550 --> 04:16.590
I want to quit.

04:16.590 --> 04:20.440
Well, if you did quit, 
that would help me quite a—

04:21.070 --> 04:24.410
You can say that now, but not for long!

04:24.880 --> 04:25.700
What?

04:26.240 --> 04:27.450
Was that a bruise?

04:32.210 --> 04:33.610
What is this?

04:33.610 --> 04:34.620
What?

04:35.020 --> 04:37.540
This is wrong. This isn't it at all.

04:38.230 --> 04:39.840
What is it that's wrong?

04:40.220 --> 04:41.260
Everything!

04:41.260 --> 04:42.420
Everything?

04:43.630 --> 04:45.390
That can't be true!

04:45.390 --> 04:48.680
I've checked the paintings countless times 
to make it as alike as possible!

04:48.680 --> 04:49.560
And still!

04:50.100 --> 04:52.640
Everything is <i>wrong</i>.

04:52.960 --> 04:54.350
This sham of an imitation...

04:55.460 --> 04:57.060
I don't even want to look at it!

05:09.490 --> 05:11.180
Give it form.

05:13.400 --> 05:15.580
You will give it form.

05:19.320 --> 05:21.580
Pull yourself together, Anne!

05:23.330 --> 05:26.010
Was it the Duke of Philax who did this?

05:26.010 --> 05:27.340
Yeah.

05:30.440 --> 05:31.470
Are you all right?

05:33.280 --> 05:35.930
No matter how many you make, 
he won't be satisfied.

05:36.650 --> 05:38.900
It's time to withdraw and leave this place.

05:41.240 --> 05:43.470
Does that mean giving up?

05:43.470 --> 05:44.440
It does.

05:44.440 --> 05:47.320
Anne, I think quitting's for the best, too.

05:47.820 --> 05:50.060
It's a shame about the thousand cress, but...

05:50.890 --> 05:52.620
Give up on the work?

05:53.370 --> 05:54.890
Even though I'm the one who accepted it?

05:56.210 --> 05:58.670
Some things are just impossible, you know?

05:58.970 --> 06:00.430
What he desires...

06:00.430 --> 06:02.620
may be something which can't be 
created in a sugar confection,

06:02.620 --> 06:04.630
something which greatly 
deviates from the norm.

06:11.990 --> 06:13.220
No...

06:13.580 --> 06:14.920
That can't be true.

06:15.340 --> 06:17.980
Otherwise, he wouldn't have
 had that look on his face.

06:18.860 --> 06:20.690
I'm going to keep going!

06:20.690 --> 06:23.030
Though, I'm sorry to make you worry about me.

06:30.610 --> 06:32.110
Oh right. Challe.

06:32.110 --> 06:34.030
Why don't you sleep in the bed tonight?

06:34.490 --> 06:36.780
I'll sleep on the floor instead.

06:36.780 --> 06:38.000
I refuse.

06:38.000 --> 06:40.490
Mithril Lid Pod's snoring is too loud.

06:44.150 --> 06:45.030
Say...

06:45.420 --> 06:47.670
how long have you been so bitter?

06:48.160 --> 06:49.980
After living over a hundred years,

06:49.980 --> 06:52.640
anyone who isn't a little bitter is naïve.

06:52.640 --> 06:54.100
A hundred years?!

06:54.570 --> 06:57.870
Though, even if you lived a hundred years, 
you don't seem like you'd change.

06:57.870 --> 06:59.370
What's that supposed to mean?

07:00.180 --> 07:02.040
<i>But, that makes sense.</i>

07:02.620 --> 07:04.460
<i>Challe's lived over a hundred years.</i>

07:04.920 --> 07:08.150
<i>Living that long, he'd have met 
lots of people, and of course...</i>

07:13.410 --> 07:14.530
Say...

07:14.840 --> 07:17.660
What was Liz like?

07:17.660 --> 07:18.860
Was she beautiful?

07:19.520 --> 07:20.680
Let's see...

07:21.600 --> 07:23.240
I believe that she was beautiful.

07:23.240 --> 07:26.260
What color were her eyes? 
Did she have long hair?

07:26.680 --> 07:27.860
Was she kind?

07:30.150 --> 07:31.910
She had blue eyes.

07:32.320 --> 07:33.750
Her hair was long.

07:34.270 --> 07:37.610
More than being kind, she was mature...

07:38.140 --> 07:40.900
quiet and thoughtful.

07:42.280 --> 07:43.530
I see.

07:45.720 --> 07:47.620
<i>She was completely different from me.</i>

07:48.180 --> 07:52.470
<i>I'm not pretty. I'm childish. I'm boisterous.</i>

07:53.200 --> 07:55.450
<i>And I never think hard enough about anything.</i>

07:57.300 --> 07:58.300
What's wrong?

07:58.300 --> 07:59.060
What?

08:06.320 --> 08:07.290
Huh?

08:07.290 --> 08:09.390
What? What is all this?

08:09.390 --> 08:11.440
Did I say something to upset you?

08:11.440 --> 08:13.160
No! Not at all!

08:13.160 --> 08:15.760
I'm sorry! I might have gotten 
something in my eye.

08:15.760 --> 08:17.580
I'm just going to go wash my face!

08:22.890 --> 08:26.070
Honestly. Why did I go and cry like that?

08:28.150 --> 08:30.110
When I get back, 
I have to apologize to Challe.

08:31.410 --> 08:33.190
What? The door is open.

08:34.270 --> 08:35.380
Challe?

08:36.160 --> 08:37.370
Hey there, Anne.

08:38.720 --> 08:41.530
Jonas! Why are you in my room?

08:41.930 --> 08:42.940
Say...

08:42.940 --> 08:45.170
do you know what this is?

08:46.120 --> 08:47.630
That wing!

08:47.630 --> 08:50.700
I'm sorry, Anne. I was sleeping and...

08:53.800 --> 08:54.750
Stop it!

08:54.750 --> 08:58.040
If you don't like me, then you should hurt me!

08:58.040 --> 09:00.430
There isn't anything I want to do to you.

09:00.430 --> 09:03.260
Though there is something 
I want you to do for me.

09:03.260 --> 09:04.630
Me?

09:04.630 --> 09:07.520
Anne, I want you to ask something of Challe.

09:07.520 --> 09:09.900
Say, "I don't want you with me anymore."

09:09.900 --> 09:13.840
"Leave this castle, and never 
appear before me again."

09:13.840 --> 09:16.260
I could never do something like—

09:16.260 --> 09:17.110
Stop it!

09:17.450 --> 09:20.740
If you do as I say, I'll give it back to you.

09:22.060 --> 09:25.500
But if you tell Challe about this, 
I'll <i>rip it to shreds</i>!

09:26.040 --> 09:27.290
<i>Jonas...</i>

09:28.120 --> 09:29.290
<i>You're...</i>

09:31.520 --> 09:33.710
<i>That girl. What was that?</i>

09:34.220 --> 09:36.110
<i>Asking about Liz...</i>

09:36.110 --> 09:37.480
<i>Suddenly starting to cry...</i>

09:37.880 --> 09:39.190
<i>It doesn't make any sense.</i>

09:44.240 --> 09:46.030
So, you came back.

09:46.030 --> 09:46.750
Challe.

09:46.750 --> 09:48.440
I have a request of you.

09:49.160 --> 09:51.140
I want you to leave here.

09:53.640 --> 09:55.400
You want me to sleep in a different room?

09:56.760 --> 09:58.900
I want to you leave this castle.

09:59.420 --> 10:03.350
And I don't want you to 
ever appear before me again.

10:04.290 --> 10:07.480
Does that mean that you don't want to 
stay together anymore?

10:13.600 --> 10:14.500
For what reason?

10:15.270 --> 10:18.390
It isn't your fault, Challe. It's mine.

10:19.220 --> 10:21.720
I'm sorry. Please, don't ask.

10:24.420 --> 10:25.510
All right.

10:36.720 --> 10:39.130
That was well done, Anne.

10:42.360 --> 10:44.180
Why would you make me do something like this?

10:45.240 --> 10:46.630
Give the wing back.

10:47.120 --> 10:48.230
Not yet.

10:49.630 --> 10:53.210
Tomorrow, you and I will meet 
with the Duke of Philax,

10:53.210 --> 10:58.000
and you will not oppose a single thing I say.

10:58.000 --> 11:01.020
You just need to do exactly as I tell you to.

11:01.710 --> 11:03.450
What are you planning to do?

11:04.030 --> 11:06.170
You'll see. Tomorrow.

11:10.120 --> 11:12.520
I'm sorry. It's all because of me.

11:12.930 --> 11:14.330
No, it's not.

11:14.330 --> 11:16.380
Jonas is the one in the wrong here.

11:16.380 --> 11:17.440
But...

11:17.720 --> 11:20.490
Anne, you love 
Challe fenn Challe, and you had to...

11:20.490 --> 11:22.110
That's not...

11:22.110 --> 11:26.040
Don't try to hide it now! 
Who do you think I am?

11:27.920 --> 11:29.160
You do, don't you?

11:29.660 --> 11:30.840
Love him.

11:34.930 --> 11:35.960
Challe...

11:41.240 --> 11:42.410
<i>Perhaps everything...</i>

11:43.050 --> 11:44.980
<i>is like this.</i>

11:47.590 --> 11:48.620
<i>Suddenly...</i>

11:49.380 --> 11:50.560
<i>it ends.</i>

12:39.190 --> 12:40.790
<i>Where should I go?</i>

12:44.930 --> 12:47.750
This is a top-quality companion fairy.

12:50.620 --> 12:53.320
Boss! This isn't a companion fairy!

12:53.320 --> 12:56.140
Doesn't change the fact 
that it'll sell for a high price.

12:56.140 --> 12:58.170
I am currently in a bad mood.

12:58.840 --> 13:00.210
I'm not responsible for what happens to you.

13:08.840 --> 13:11.180
That's enough, Challe fenn Challe.

13:11.180 --> 13:13.890
If you kill a human, 
I won't be able to protect you.

13:14.570 --> 13:18.360
And you lot, I'll pretend I didn't see this, 
so hurry up and get lost!

13:18.860 --> 13:21.400
Why are you here, Layabout Viscount?

13:21.400 --> 13:25.850
As usual, you aren't at all endearing. 
Rejoice at our coincidental reunion.

13:27.720 --> 13:29.160
Where are Anne and Mithril?

13:29.830 --> 13:31.860
I asked my question first.

13:33.600 --> 13:35.960
I have business at Philax Castle.

13:36.850 --> 13:39.290
You three were there, too, weren't you?

13:41.170 --> 13:45.060
Doesn't matter. Since we have run into 
each other, won't you come with me?

13:46.080 --> 13:48.260
Left as he is, 
the Duke of Philax is in danger.

13:51.720 --> 13:53.110
Why are you here?

13:54.150 --> 13:56.700
I've come to ask a boon of you.

13:57.160 --> 13:58.440
<i>Listen.</i>

13:58.440 --> 14:00.770
Do not oppose a single thing.

14:00.770 --> 14:03.730
What I mean is, do exactly as I say.

14:04.760 --> 14:07.850
I ask you to allow me to quit my work here.

14:14.000 --> 14:17.220
You said the same thing 
the other day, didn't you?

14:17.840 --> 14:18.630
Yes, Your Grace.

14:19.230 --> 14:21.500
What did I tell you then?

14:22.180 --> 14:23.920
That quitting...

14:23.920 --> 14:25.740
would not be permitted.

14:26.190 --> 14:27.320
That's right.

14:28.520 --> 14:31.430
Try to escape and I'll have you in chains.

14:31.430 --> 14:32.600
<i>What?</i>

14:32.600 --> 14:34.510
I believe I told you that as well.

14:34.840 --> 14:36.490
If you've forgotten,

14:36.490 --> 14:38.580
then as you feel this pain once more...

14:39.230 --> 14:40.690
you will remember.

14:42.000 --> 14:42.770
<i>Could it be?</i>

14:43.280 --> 14:44.480
<i>Was that bruise...</i>

14:44.950 --> 14:46.410
Please, have mercy on me!

14:46.410 --> 14:48.200
I can't make anything more!

14:48.200 --> 14:49.980
But Anne will stay!

14:49.980 --> 14:53.450
You can have her stay until the sugar 
confection is done, and no one will mind!

14:53.760 --> 14:55.690
I drove her warrior fairy away!

14:55.690 --> 14:58.570
So, please! Please allow me to leave!

14:58.570 --> 14:59.120
I beg of you!

14:59.120 --> 15:00.300
You're still saying that?

15:00.300 --> 15:01.080
I beg of you!

15:01.080 --> 15:04.540
I beg of you! I beg of you! I beg of you!

15:04.540 --> 15:05.690
I beg of you!

15:07.200 --> 15:10.170
Your Grace, it is just as he says.

15:10.170 --> 15:11.010
What?

15:11.010 --> 15:12.220
Anne...

15:12.510 --> 15:14.930
I will, without fail, 
make you a sugar confection.

15:15.280 --> 15:17.640
So, please, allow this person to leave.

15:18.440 --> 15:19.920
Without fail?

15:19.920 --> 15:20.660
Yes, Your Grace.

15:21.120 --> 15:24.350
If you can't, I will never allow you 
to leave this castle.

15:24.350 --> 15:25.480
That will be fine.

15:26.480 --> 15:28.460
I made you a promise.

15:28.460 --> 15:29.190
That is why...

15:29.580 --> 15:31.020
I will continue to create.

15:33.240 --> 15:34.530
Very well.

15:34.910 --> 15:36.330
You will make it...

15:36.990 --> 15:38.310
without fail!

15:39.960 --> 15:42.880
You're really going to make something?

15:42.880 --> 15:45.930
For him, who only ever says, "That's wrong"?

15:45.930 --> 15:49.660
I don't want to be someone like you, 
who abandons things halfway.

15:50.090 --> 15:51.300
That's why I will make it.

15:52.300 --> 15:54.760
You're strange. 
There's something wrong with you.

15:54.760 --> 15:56.550
That's right! You're stupid!

15:58.310 --> 15:59.740
Huh? What do you want?

15:59.740 --> 16:02.090
Give it back. Mithril's wing.

16:02.090 --> 16:03.770
Oh, that's right.

16:06.780 --> 16:07.580
Goodbye, then.

16:08.420 --> 16:09.770
<i>I will make it.</i>

16:11.000 --> 16:12.380
<i>I will make the sugar confection.</i>

16:13.290 --> 16:14.660
<i>Because that...</i>

16:15.780 --> 16:17.370
<i>is my work.</i>

16:19.040 --> 16:21.130
Maybe it's because you always have
 such a frightening look on your face...

16:21.130 --> 16:22.910
that Anne cast you aside.

16:24.210 --> 16:26.220
And what's that with your legs 
supposed to mean?

16:26.880 --> 16:28.010
This is tiresome.

16:29.090 --> 16:31.520
I know you're on edge.

16:31.520 --> 16:34.580
Why are you going to the castle? 
What is this danger you speak of?

16:36.690 --> 16:39.140
There's a smell of smoke about things.

16:39.560 --> 16:42.490
And if Anne is still there, that isn't good.

16:47.940 --> 16:49.150
For the last year and a half,

16:49.600 --> 16:52.790
the Duke of Philax hasn't 
shown his face in Lewiston.

16:53.210 --> 16:54.840
You know what that means, right?

16:55.370 --> 16:58.800
He's been shirking his duty 
to show fealty to the royal family.

16:58.800 --> 16:59.990
Is that right?

17:00.560 --> 17:02.410
I don't know the reason for it.

17:02.410 --> 17:07.530
But the Earl of Downing finds it unforgivable 
and has requested the duke's subjugation.

17:07.530 --> 17:10.960
His Majesty was overcome in the end 
and had to give his permission.

17:11.310 --> 17:12.730
Which is why, if we don't hurry,

17:12.730 --> 17:15.370
the earl will come to Philax, 
and bring soldiers with him.

17:16.190 --> 17:18.650
But I don't want the duke to die.

17:19.240 --> 17:23.850
Before I became the Silver Sugar Viscount, 
I often went to see the duke,

17:24.300 --> 17:28.380
so that I could make sugar confections 
for the woman at his side.

17:30.900 --> 17:33.770
That's why I know his nature.

17:35.000 --> 17:37.200
And why I know he has no ambitions.

17:40.320 --> 17:42.790
It has been quite some time, Duke of Philax.

17:43.540 --> 17:45.040
What have you come here for?

17:45.480 --> 17:47.800
To invite you on a journey. To Lewiston.

17:48.360 --> 17:50.860
So that's it. I'm not going.

17:51.330 --> 17:52.650
It will be fun.

17:52.650 --> 17:54.070
You call that fun?

17:56.200 --> 17:57.380
Sir!

17:57.920 --> 18:01.070
The Earl of Downing 
is headed here with soldiers.

18:01.070 --> 18:03.310
But His Majesty doesn't 
truly wish for your subjugation.

18:04.560 --> 18:06.430
You still have time!

18:07.080 --> 18:08.270
So, please, come with me to Lewiston!

18:08.270 --> 18:10.020
I said, I'm not going.

18:11.120 --> 18:15.360
I know! What if Lady Christina 
accompanied you?

18:15.360 --> 18:18.060
She liked Lewiston, didn't she?

18:18.060 --> 18:19.630
That's right. That would be good.

18:19.630 --> 18:20.570
Leave.

18:20.920 --> 18:21.830
What?

18:22.500 --> 18:24.480
I'm telling you to leave!

18:31.290 --> 18:33.820
What's wrong, Sir?

18:33.820 --> 18:39.010
No one commands me! 
No one tells <i>me</i> what <i>I</i> should do!

18:39.360 --> 18:40.340
That goes for you, too!

18:40.340 --> 18:41.750
Mercury!

18:48.840 --> 18:50.660
Argh!

18:51.330 --> 18:52.540
My neck!

18:53.440 --> 18:54.440
I'm sorry!

18:54.440 --> 18:56.780
You could have waited in our rooms.

18:56.780 --> 18:58.270
Would I do that?

18:58.270 --> 19:01.030
The only one who can guide your way 
right now is the magnificent me!

19:01.970 --> 19:03.050
I see.

19:07.380 --> 19:10.870
Why do you think it has to be this fairy?

19:11.180 --> 19:13.050
That's a good question.

19:13.050 --> 19:15.180
I wonder if there's some reason for it.

19:34.120 --> 19:34.980
What?

19:39.010 --> 19:40.300
This is...

19:42.360 --> 19:44.790
Why didn't I notice it?

19:45.960 --> 19:47.640
She has two wings!

19:48.150 --> 19:51.820
This fairy has never been made 
to serve anyone.

19:53.200 --> 19:56.380
Why would a portrait of a fairy 
like that be hanging here?

19:56.830 --> 20:02.070
<i>Perhaps the Duke of Philax isn't simply 
looking for a splendid sugar confection.</i>

20:02.790 --> 20:04.220
I must ask him.

20:04.220 --> 20:07.260
I must ask His Grace about this fairy!

20:07.260 --> 20:08.810
Are you serious, Anne?

20:09.160 --> 20:12.270
Going to see someone 
who's lost his sanity like that is...

20:12.270 --> 20:15.080
And just because it's you 
doesn't mean he won't...

20:15.080 --> 20:17.230
Say, Mithril Lid Pod.

20:17.230 --> 20:18.730
You should leave this castle too.

20:19.020 --> 20:19.660
What?!

20:19.660 --> 20:21.640
I can't escape on my own and leave you here!

20:21.640 --> 20:24.200
But you might be put in danger.

20:24.850 --> 20:29.160
This is my work, so I'm the only one 
who needs to stay.

20:29.160 --> 20:30.560
Anne...

20:30.560 --> 20:33.560
When I've finished the sugar confection, 
I'll come and find you. Just wait.

20:36.480 --> 20:38.630
All right! I'll leave the castle!

20:38.630 --> 20:42.280
But the reason I'm leaving is 
to find Challe fenn Challe!

20:42.280 --> 20:46.340
Then I'll tell him that you didn't mean 
all those things you said!

20:46.340 --> 20:49.240
The magnificence that is I 
will find him, without fail!

20:49.240 --> 20:51.620
Thank you. I'm counting on you!

20:54.600 --> 20:55.750
<i>I must go...</i>

20:56.400 --> 20:58.200
<i>to the duke!</i>

20:58.990 --> 21:04.950
A False Farewell

21:16.210 --> 21:20.540
<i>Is it just like the dreams we dream at night?</i>

21:21.410 --> 21:26.680
<i>Do we give names to our other dreams because,</i>

21:26.680 --> 21:30.220
<i>Just as our night dreams 
are forgotten upon waking,</i>

21:30.220 --> 21:37.290
<i>If they aren't held dear, 
they will disappear?</i>

21:37.290 --> 21:48.430
<i>No, it's because they aren't things 
that only special people can see</i>

21:48.430 --> 21:49.160
<i>That day</i>

21:49.160 --> 21:53.610
<i>I reached out again and again</i>

21:53.610 --> 21:59.170
<i>I failed to catch that shining fruit, and yet</i>

21:59.170 --> 22:04.670
<i>I'll reach out once more</i>

22:04.670 --> 22:08.970
<i>If I make my wishes come true myself</i>

22:08.970 --> 22:14.800
<i>I just know it will make you smile</i>

22:14.800 --> 22:26.280
<i>That's why I'm able to say I'm not giving up</i>

22:36.040 --> 22:40.000
<b>If I Keep Gazing at You</b>
